  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="0362d7d3-c1bc-5fbe-b76c-a96cd1364f1e" activityNameId="28a3758c-7841-5caa-b3d5-a7b16175cad8" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Cadmium, primary, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Cadmium, primary, at plant
The module describes the primary production of cadmium metal (99.9%) on a global average. No secondary sources from post consumer scrap are considered. Only the most important source, the cadmium sludges from hydrometallurgical zinc operations, is reflected with the dataset. For the use in applications where cadmium is a major constituent – e.g. in NiCd battery systems – the dataset should be complemented with additional specific emission factors and the secondary production process.;
CAS number: 007440-43-9; 
Formula: Cd; 
UUID: 7f656f5c-03d0-3716-bb6b-184bdcf2379c
The module includes the treatment of cadmium sludge from hydrometallurgical zinc operations and subsequent refining by electrolysis. Transports and infrastructure are considered.
Location: This module represents the production of primary cadmium on a global average. The inventory however is compiled with European average data, e.g. for electricity production.
Technology: Cadmium sludge formed in hydrometallurgical zinc operations by purification of zinc solution. Subsequent purification and oxidation of the sponge. Cadmium cathodes formed by electrowinning. Other sources from pyrometallurgical zinc wastes and post consumer scrap (batteries) disregarded.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: 20'900 t in 2006
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_7f656f5c-03d0-3716-bb6b-184bdcf2379c.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
